Key Market Drivers
1. Regulatory Tightening Around Electromagnetic Compatibility
Governments and standards bodies worldwide are revising EMC directives to address the proliferation of high‑frequency wireless technologies. Updated IEC 61000 and FCC rules increase the stringency of emission limits for consumer electronics, automotive systems and aerospace platforms. Manufacturers are compelled to invest in more precise and higher‑frequency test equipment to avoid costly redesign cycles and market delays.
2. Growth of Connected Devices in Industrial Sectors
The surge in IoT‑enabled machinery, autonomous vehicles and smart‑factory automation raises the electromagnetic interference (EMI) risk profile across production lines. Operators are adopting continuous‑monitoring solutions-such as AI‑enhanced spectrum analyzers-to detect transient emissions in real time, thereby safeguarding line uptime and product quality.
